{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"reasoning","text":"**Gathering evidence for claims**\n\nI'm thinking I need to gather some exact source excerpts to back up my claims. I should create evidence items with concrete artifacts like formal arguments, statistical results, or model constraints. I have a few potential claims lined up. For instance, I could discuss how PCA-perturbed impostor planes reduce viewpoint-popping artifacts while managing distortions. Other claims focus on optimizing memory usage, improving animation compression, and enhancing visual effects using various techniques.\n**Analyzing rendering performance**\n\nI'm considering how the implementation managed to render 10,000 different humans in a 41,260-polygon village at frame rates between 12-20 fps. It seems the scalability drops to about 26.20 fps at zero, 24.08 fps with 1,000, 18.26 fps at 5,000, and 13.35 fps at 10,000. This indicates that the frame-time relation is nearly linear with crowd size. The resources needed for rendering static city elements are substantial, which leads me to think I might have eight claims to support."}}
