{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"find verification/example_site/spaces/graphics/sources verification/example_site/spaces/graphics/claims -maxdepth 1 -type f -print | sort | xargs -r sed -n '1,220p'\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:44:00Z\",\n  \"claim_id\": \"claim-a-regular-grid-of-environment-tiles-can-support-both-collision-behavior-and-shad--202b441327e8\",\n  \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n    \"To control the virtual humans\\u2019 motion, we subdivided the floor of the environment into regular-sized tiles.\",\n    \"Several types of information can be stored, but presently, we only use this information for collision detection and shadowing.\"\n  ],\n  \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n  \"short_title\": \"Grid tiles guide motion\",\n  \"source_id\": \"source-02-image-based-crowd-rendering--565ae2b0e3a1\",\n  \"text\": \"A regular grid of environment tiles can support both collision behavior and shadowing decisions for moving virtual humans.\"\n}\n{\n  \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:36:26Z\",\n  \"claim_id\": \"claim-a-shader-is-a-gpu-directed-program-that-describes-rendering-processes-for-turnin--64c2250afac1\",\n  \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n    \"Le shadercoding d\\u00e9signe l'action de coder un shader. Celui-ci est un programme s'adressant directement \\u00e0 la carte graphique, aussi appel\\u00e9 GPU pour Graphic Processing Unit, de l'ordinateur sur lequel il est ex\\u00e9cut\\u00e9. Il d\\u00e9crit chaque \\u00e9tape du rendu, c'est-\\u00e0-dire chaque processus qui vont permettre \\u00e0 la machine d'afficher une image en fonction des informations des points dans l'espace 3D et de leurs propri\\u00e9t\\u00e9s physiques.\"\n  ],\n  \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n  \"short_title\": \"Shaders direct GPU rendering\",\n  \"source_id\": \"source-01-sphere-tracing-a-geometric-method-for-the-antialiased-ray-tracing-of-implicit-surfaces--eee351440d34\",\n  \"text\": \"A shader is a GPU-directed program that describes rendering processes for turning 3D spatial data and physical properties into an image.\"\n}\n{\n  \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:44:00Z\",\n  \"claim_id\": \"claim-alpha-channel-multipass-rendering-can-recolor-significant-body-regions-such-as-c--265615107527\",\n  \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n    \"We performed multipass rendering using the alpha channel to select the parts to render. For each pass, we change the impostor polygon color to the desired color.\",\n    \"Computing a texture modulation preserves the shading because it\\u2019s already included in the texture.\"\n  ],\n  \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n  \"short_title\": \"Multipass coloring diversifies avatars\",\n  \"source_id\": \"source-02-image-based-crowd-rendering--565ae2b0e3a1\",\n  \"text\": \"Alpha-channel multipass rendering can recolor significant body regions such as clothes, hair, and skin to increase avatar variety while preserving baked texture shading.\"\n}\n{\n  \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:36:26Z\",\n  \"claim_id\": \"claim-creating-original-shaders-requires-substantial-mathematical-and-technical-fluenc--7ec21177eabc\",\n  \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n    \"Un shader se d\\u00e9crit donc \\u00e0 l'aide de ph\\u00e9nom\\u00e8nes physiques et math\\u00e9matiques parfois complexes, faisant appel aux matrices et leurs transform\\u00e9es, ou encore aux vecteurs et aux diff\\u00e9rentes op\\u00e9rations possibles entre eux. Il faut alors avoir une base de connaissances scientifiques et techniques relativement pouss\\u00e9e, si l'on souhaite coder ses propres shaders.\"\n  ],\n  \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n  \"short_title\": \"Shadercraft requires mathematical fluency\",\n  \"source_id\": \"source-01-sphere-tracing-a-geometric-method-for-the-antialiased-ray-tracing-of-implicit-surfaces--eee351440d34\",\n  \"text\": \"Creating original shaders requires substantial mathematical and technical fluency in functions, vectors, matrices, and spatial reasoning.\"\n}\n{\n  \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:36:26Z\",\n  \"claim_id\": \"claim-digital-art-practice-must-negotiate-the-tension-between-scientific-technical-pro--0ddadf7f5e3d\",\n  \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n    \"L'artiste num\\u00e9rique veut exprimer une sensation, un v\\u00e9cu, cr\\u00e9er du sensible au travers de machines logiques, r\\u00e9fl\\u00e9chissant \\u00e0 base de 0 et de 1. Une r\\u00e9flexion logique et technique en amont est donc toujours n\\u00e9cessaire pour r\\u00e9aliser une \\u0153uvre num\\u00e9rique.\"\n  ],\n  \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n  \"short_title\": \"Digital art bridges calculation\",\n  \"source_id\": \"source-01-sphere-tracing-a-geometric-method-for-the-antialiased-ray-tracing-of-implicit-surfaces--eee351440d34\",\n  \"text\": \"Digital art practice must negotiate the tension between scientific-technical processes and the desire to produce sensible artistic experience.\"\n}\n{\n  \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:36:26Z\",\n  \"claim_id\": \"claim-fragment-shaders-map-two-dimensional-pixel-positions-to-colors-and-can-generate--ff479c9f654e\",\n  \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n    \"Pour r\\u00e9sumer, celui-ci va prendre en entr\\u00e9e la position d'un \\u00ab point num\\u00e9rique \\u00bb de l'espace 2D, appel\\u00e9 pixel, et va retourner une couleur pour le pixel correspondant. ... Mais la propri\\u00e9t\\u00e9 premi\\u00e8re du fragment shader peut aussi permettre de g\\u00e9n\\u00e9rer, \\u00e0 l'aide de formules math\\u00e9matiques, des motifs ou patterns particuliers. Ceux-ci peuvent \\u00eatre anim\\u00e9s avec des variables \\u00e9voluant dans le temps ou selon d'autres informations externes.\"\n  ],\n  \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n  \"short_title\": \"Fragment shaders generate patterns\",\n  \"source_id\": \"source-01-sphere-tracing-a-geometric-method-for-the-antialiased-ray-tracing-of-implicit-surfaces--eee351440d34\",\n  \"text\": \"Fragment shaders map two-dimensional pixel positions to colors and can generate animated mathematical patterns responsive to time or external inputs.\"\n}\n{\n  \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:44:00Z\",\n  \"claim_id\": \"claim-image-based-impostor-rendering-with-positional-and-directional-discretization-ca--3b5de902e034\",\n  \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n    \"To display many different individual people at interactive frame rates, we combined texture compression with multipass rendering.\",\n    \"Our system allows real-time rendering of densely populated large-scale environments. The rendering speed is independent of the avatar model\\u2019s complexity.\"\n  ],\n  \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n  \"short_title\": \"Impostors enable real-time crowds\",\n  \"source_id\": \"source-02-image-based-crowd-rendering--565ae2b0e3a1\",\n  \"text\": \"Image-based impostor rendering with positional and directional discretization can display dense animated crowds in large virtual urban environments at interactive rates.\"\n}\n{\n  \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:36:26Z\",\n  \"claim_id\": \"claim-mastered-shadercoding-can-support-real-time-artistic-improvisation-that-fuses-co--51c4a707f8d0\",\n  \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n    \"Tout cela \\u00e9tait possible aussi car j'avais de la marge pour improviser et \\u00eatre impulsive du fait de ma ma\\u00eetrise du langage et de la technicit\\u00e9 de cette programmation. J'avais trouv\\u00e9 le moyen technique me correspondant et me permettant de \\u00ab faire na\\u00eetre une \\u0153uvre \\u00bb, par la communion entre le code (la technique), l'image et l'\\u00e9change.\"\n  ],\n  \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n  \"short_title\": \"Mastery enables live improvisation\",\n  \"source_id\": \"source-01-sphere-tracing-a-geometric-method-for-the-antialiased-ray-tracing-of-implicit-surfaces--eee351440d34\",\n  \"text\": \"Mastered shadercoding can support real-time artistic improvisation that fuses code, image, performer, and audience into a live digital performance.\"\n}\n{\n  \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:36:26Z\",\n  \"claim_id\": \"claim-mathematical-and-technical-constraints-in-shadercoding-can-become-creative-motor--5b703448e7f5\",\n  \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n    \"Ces propos d'Alain nous montre une autre voie de la pratique de l'art num\\u00e9rique : les contraintes peuvent \\u00eatre cr\\u00e9atrices. Ce qui nous est impos\\u00e9 peut nous diriger dans notre cr\\u00e9ativit\\u00e9. La technicit\\u00e9 derri\\u00e8re le shadercoding peut donc \\u00eatre cr\\u00e9atrice, elle peut \\u00eatre un moteur de celle-ci.\"\n  ],\n  \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n  \"short_title\": \"Constraints drive shader creativity\",\n  \"source_id\": \"source-01-sphere-tracing-a-geometric-method-for-the-antialiased-ray-tracing-of-implicit-surfaces--eee351440d34\",\n  \"text\": \"Mathematical and technical constraints in shadercoding can become creative motors rather than merely limiting conditions.\"\n}\n{\n  \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:44:00Z\",\n  \"claim_id\": \"claim-opengl-compressed-textures-and-compact-frame-storage-allow-ten-human-types-with--0cc37130330a\",\n  \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n    \"We then stored the texture using the OpenGL compressed format, which gives a further memory compression ratio of 1:4.\",\n    \"To simulate 10 different types of human with 10 frames of animation each, we need about 25 Mbytes of texture memory.\"\n  ],\n  \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n  \"short_title\": \"Compressed textures enable variety\",\n  \"source_id\": \"source-02-image-based-crowd-rendering--565ae2b0e3a1\",\n  \"text\": \"OpenGL compressed textures and compact frame storage allow ten human types with ten animation frames each to fit in about 25 Mbytes of texture memory.\"\n}\n{\n  \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:44:00Z\",\n  \"claim_id\": \"claim-packing-each-prerendered-human-sample-into-the-smallest-containing-rectangle-red--c2027548dc18\",\n  \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n    \"Thanks to this process, the resulting new image is much smaller than the original without any loss of image quality.\",\n    \"With our current reorganization strategy, we can reduce the amount of texture memory necessary to store our human images to 25 percent of the original value.\"\n  ],\n  \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n  \"short_title\": \"Sample packing cuts memory\",\n  \"source_id\": \"source-02-image-based-crowd-rendering--565ae2b0e3a1\",\n  \"text\": \"Packing each prerendered human sample into the smallest containing rectangle reduces the texture memory needed for human images to one quarter of the original value without loss of image quality.\"\n}\n{\n  \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:44:00Z\",\n  \"claim_id\": \"claim-perturbing-an-impostor-plane-toward-a-pca-derived-best-fitting-plane-reduces-vie--e9f84568a82e\",\n  \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n    \"Starting from an impostor plane purely perpendicular to the camera, we \\u201cperturbed\\u201d its orientation using the resulting plane obtained from a PCA of the sample image. This minimized the popping while limiting the introduction of other artifacts.\"\n  ],\n  \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n  \"short_title\": \"PCA planes reduce popping\",\n  \"source_id\": \"source-02-image-based-crowd-rendering--565ae2b0e3a1\",\n  \"text\": \"Perturbing an impostor plane toward a PCA-derived best-fitting plane reduces viewpoint-change popping for walking human impostors while limiting newly introduced distortions.\"\n}\n{\n  \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:36:26Z\",\n  \"claim_id\": \"claim-raymarching-can-recreate-three-dimensional-depth-inside-a-fragment-shader-by-mar--eb7e615f4e18\",\n  \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n    \"Une technique permet m\\u00eame de recr\\u00e9er de la profondeur dans le fragment shader et donc d'afficher \\u00e0 nouveau de la 3D : le raymarching. ... Il s'agit de d\\u00e9crire l'espace selon des fonctions de distances en un point donn\\u00e9 ... Ensuite, pour chaque pixel de l'image, on lance un rayon sur lequel on va 'marcher' pas \\u00e0 pas ... rencontrer un objet d\\u00e9crit dans la fonction de distance (appel\\u00e9e commun\\u00e9ment SDF pour Signed Distance Field).\"\n  ],\n  \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n  \"short_title\": \"Raymarching recreates shader depth\",\n  \"source_id\": \"source-01-sphere-tracing-a-geometric-method-for-the-antialiased-ray-tracing-of-implicit-surfaces--eee351440d34\",\n  \"text\": \"Raymarching can recreate three-dimensional depth inside a fragment shader by marching a ray through a distance-field description until it reaches an object.\"\n}\n{\n  \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:36:26Z\",\n  \"claim_id\": \"claim-shader-showdowns-turn-shadercoding-into-a-timed-public-performance-evaluated-thr--a575bceeaf8e\",\n  \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n    \"Plus commun\\u00e9ment appel\\u00e9 Shader Showdown, il s'agit de coder son effet visuel \\u00e0 l'aide d'un shader en 25 ou 30 minutes devant un public. Suite \\u00e0 cette \\u00e9preuve, les participants seront jug\\u00e9s par les spectateurs sur diff\\u00e9rents crit\\u00e8res : l'image finale produite, la technicit\\u00e9 du code mais \\u00e9galement l'\\u00e9volution de l'effet au cours de l'\\u00e9preuve.\"\n  ],\n  \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n  \"short_title\": \"Showdowns stage shader performance\",\n  \"source_id\": \"source-01-sphere-tracing-a-geometric-method-for-the-antialiased-ray-tracing-of-implicit-surfaces--eee351440d34\",\n  \"text\": \"Shader Showdowns turn shadercoding into a timed public performance evaluated through the final image, code technique, and visual evolution during the event.\"\n}\n{\n  \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:36:26Z\",\n  \"claim_id\": \"claim-shadercoding-blends-programming-mathematics-and-graphics-into-a-digital-art-prac--ba3619b7f801\",\n  \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n    \"Dans un contexte o\\u00f9 l'art num\\u00e9rique est de plus en plus pr\\u00e9sent, il convient de questionner certains de ses aspects, notamment celui du profil de l'artiste technique. Pour se faire, cet article propose une introduction th\\u00e9orique au shadercoding, une discipline m\\u00ealant programmation, math\\u00e9matiques et graphisme, mais \\u00e9galement une r\\u00e9flexion sur la performance d'art num\\u00e9rique au travers de cette pratique, dans des \\u00e9v\\u00e9nements de programmation en temps-r\\u00e9el.\"\n  ],\n  \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n  \"short_title\": \"Shadercoding blends code and art\",\n  \"source_id\": \"source-01-sphere-tracing-a-geometric-method-for-the-antialiased-ray-tracing-of-implicit-surfaces--eee351440d34\",\n  \"text\": \"Shadercoding blends programming, mathematics, and graphics into a digital-art practice that can be theorized technically and performatively.\"\n}\n{\n  \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:44:00Z\",\n  \"claim_id\": \"claim-the-same-image-database-used-for-impostors-can-project-posture-consistent-human--625367fc5d02\",\n  \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n    \"Using the impostor approach, we can also compute and display the moving humans\\u2019 shadows.\",\n    \"With the cost of only one additional polygon corresponding to the projection of the impostor polygon on the ground, we create a shadow corresponding to the human posture.\"\n  ],\n  \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n  \"short_title\": \"Impostors project human shadows\",\n  \"source_id\": \"source-02-image-based-crowd-rendering--565ae2b0e3a1\",\n  \"text\": \"The same image database used for impostors can project posture-consistent human shadows onto the ground at the cost of one additional polygon.\"\n}\n{\n  \"added_at\": \"2026-04-26T16:44:00Z\",\n  \"claim_id\": \"claim-the-tested-system-renders-10-000-different-humans-in-a-41-260-polygon-village-at--6845dedcbaed\",\n  \"evidence_excerpts\": [\n    \"These humans move in a village modeled with 41,260 polygons. The display updates between 12 and 20 frames per second, depending on the displayed polygonal complexity.\",\n    \"The frame per second rate for 0 people was 26.20; for 1,000 people, it was 24.08; for 5,000 people, it was 18.26; and for 10,000 people, it was 13.35.\"\n  ],\n  \"schema_version\": \"claim_record_v1\",\n  \"short_title\": \"Ten thousand humans remain interactive\",\n  \"source_id\": \"source-02-image-based-crowd-rendering--565ae2b0e3a1\",\n  \"text\": \"The tested system renders 10,000 different humans in a 41,260-polygon village at 12 to 20 frames per second, with measured frame rates falling from 26.20 fps at zero people to 13.35 fps at 10,000 people.\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"reasoning","text":"**Synthesizing technical topics**\n\nI'm looking to synthesize shared concepts from various sources without inventing anything unsupported. I can create two or three topics. \n\nOne could be \"Real-time graphics as a technical-performance medium,\" focusing on shader coding for live performances and crowd rendering. Another could cover \"Image generation through spatial sampling,\" discussing techniques like fragment shaders and raymarching. Lastly, I might explore \"Constraints as creative/visual optimization,\" showing how technical limitations can enhance visual variety in interactive performance. Each section will summarize the core ideas and source IDs.\n**Incorporating source claims**\n\nI need to make sure to include all the claims from source-02. That’ll cover image-based impostors related to topics one and two, PCA planes for topic two, and other elements like packing, OpenGL compression, and alpha multipass for topic three. I should also incorporate grid tiles and shadows for topic two, as well as the tested system in topic one. Each topic will require their respective source IDs. I'll create a schema with an array of strings for sections, simplifying the structure."}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"Evidence is sufficient for cross-source topics; now I’ll write the JSON artifact directly."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\noutput_path = Path('/Users/chrgre01/src/Sapi/verification/example_site/spaces/graphics/runs/run-20260426T163844Z--hlmvvvvg9j/semantic/topic_generation.json')\noutput_path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n\ndata = {\n    \\\"topics\\\": [\n        {\n            \\\"topic_id\\\": \\\"topic-real-time-graphics-as-performance-medium\\\",\n            \\\"title\\\": \\\"Real-time graphics as a performance medium\\\",\n            \\\"structure_type\\\": \\\"wiki\\\",\n            \\\"sections\\\": [\n                \\\"Both sources treat real-time rendering as more than offline image production: shadercoding becomes a timed public or improvisational performance, while image-based crowd rendering is judged by whether dense animated scenes remain interactive.\\\",\n                \\\"The shared concept is performance under live constraints. The shadercoding source emphasizes code, image, performer, and audience; the crowd-rendering source emphasizes frame-rate evidence for thousands of moving humans in a virtual city.\\\",\n                \\\"A topic page should keep the domains distinct: one source concerns artistic live coding, while the other concerns rendering-system engineering, but both rely on technical control to sustain real-time visual experience.\\\"\n            ],\n            \\\"claim_ids\\\": [\n                \\\"claim-shadercoding-blends-programming-mathematics-and-graphics-into-a-digital-art-prac--ba3619b7f801\\\",\n                \\\"claim-mastered-shadercoding-can-support-real-time-artistic-improvisation-that-fuses-co--51c4a707f8d0\\\",\n                \\\"claim-shader-showdowns-turn-shadercoding-into-a-timed-public-performance-evaluated-thr--a575bceeaf8e\\\",\n                \\\"claim-image-based-impostor-rendering-with-positional-and-directional-discretization-ca--3b5de902e034\\\",\n                \\\"claim-the-tested-system-renders-10-000-different-humans-in-a-41-260-polygon-village-at--6845dedcbaed\\\"\n            ],\n            \\\"source_ids\\\": [\n                \\\"source-01-sphere-tracing-a-geometric-method-for-the-antialiased-ray-tracing-of-implicit-surfaces--eee351440d34\\\",\n                \\\"source-02-image-based-crowd-rendering--565ae2b0e3a1\\\"\n            ]\n        },\n        {\n            \\\"topic_id\\\": \\\"topic-spatial-abstractions-for-interactive-images\\\",\n            \\\"title\\\": \\\"Spatial abstractions for interactive images\\\",\n            \\\"structure_type\\\": \\\"wiki\\\",\n            \\\"sections\\\": [\n                \\\"The sources share a concern with replacing full physical or geometric complexity with computable spatial abstractions that can still produce convincing images in real time.\\\",\n                \\\"In shadercoding, fragment shaders map pixel positions to colors and raymarching reconstructs depth by stepping through distance fields. In crowd rendering, impostors, directional discretization, PCA-adjusted planes, tile grids, and projected shadows approximate people, motion constraints, and lighting cues.\\\",\n                \\\"The synthesis is strongest at the level of technique rather than purpose: one source uses mathematical fields and pixels for digital-art imagery, while the other uses image samples and spatial discretization for scalable animated crowds.\\\"\n            ],\n            \\\"claim_ids\\\": [\n                \\\"claim-a-shader-is-a-gpu-directed-program-that-describes-rendering-processes-for-turnin--64c2250afac1\\\",\n                \\\"claim-fragment-shaders-map-two-dimensional-pixel-positions-to-colors-and-can-generate--ff479c9f654e\\\",\n                \\\"claim-raymarching-can-recreate-three-dimensional-depth-inside-a-fragment-shader-by-mar--eb7e615f4e18\\\",\n                \\\"claim-image-based-impostor-rendering-with-positional-and-directional-discretization-ca--3b5de902e034\\\",\n                \\\"claim-perturbing-an-impostor-plane-toward-a-pca-derived-best-fitting-plane-reduces-vie--e9f84568a82e\\\",\n                \\\"claim-a-regular-grid-of-environment-tiles-can-support-both-collision-behavior-and-shad--202b441327e8\\\",\n                \\\"claim-the-same-image-database-used-for-impostors-can-project-posture-consistent-human--625367fc5d02\\\"\n            ],\n            \\\"source_ids\\\": [\n                \\\"source-01-sphere-tracing-a-geometric-method-for-the-antialiased-ray-tracing-of-implicit-surfaces--eee351440d34\\\",\n                \\\"source-02-image-based-crowd-rendering--565ae2b0e3a1\\\"\n            ]\n        },\n        {\n            \\\"topic_id\\\": \\\"topic-technical-constraints-as-visual-generators\\\",\n            \\\"title\\\": \\\"Technical constraints as visual generators\\\",\n            \\\"structure_type\\\": \\\"wiki\\\",\n            \\\"sections\\\": [\n                \\\"Both sources frame technical limits as productive rather than merely restrictive. Shadercoding treats mathematical and programming constraints as conditions for artistic creation; crowd rendering turns memory, texture, and model-complexity limits into concrete rendering strategies.\\\",\n                \\\"The crowd-rendering evidence is operational: sample packing, OpenGL texture compression, compact animation-frame storage, and alpha-channel multipass recoloring reduce memory pressure while preserving or expanding visual variety.\\\",\n                \\\"The shadercoding evidence is conceptual and practice-oriented: mathematical fluency enables original shaders, and mastered technical constraints can become creative motors for digital art. A topic should avoid claiming the crowd-rendering paper makes an artistic argument, but can compare how constraints shape image-making in both cases.\\\"\n            ],\n            \\\"claim_ids\\\": [\n                \\\"claim-creating-original-shaders-requires-substantial-mathematical-and-technical-fluenc--7ec21177eabc\\\",\n                \\\"claim-digital-art-practice-must-negotiate-the-tension-between-scientific-technical-pro--0ddadf7f5e3d\\\",\n                \\\"claim-mathematical-and-technical-constraints-in-shadercoding-can-become-creative-motor--5b703448e7f5\\\",\n                \\\"claim-packing-each-prerendered-human-sample-into-the-smallest-containing-rectangle-red--c2027548dc18\\\",\n                \\\"claim-opengl-compressed-textures-and-compact-frame-storage-allow-ten-human-types-with--0cc37130330a\\\",\n                \\\"claim-alpha-channel-multipass-rendering-can-recolor-significant-body-regions-such-as-c--265615107527\\\"\n            ],\n            \\\"source_ids\\\": [\n                \\\"source-01-sphere-tracing-a-geometric-method-for-the-antialiased-ray-tracing-of-implicit-surfaces--eee351440d34\\\",\n                \\\"source-02-image-based-crowd-rendering--565ae2b0e3a1\\\"\n            ]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n\nwith output_path.open('w', encoding='utf-8') as file:\n    json.dump(data, file, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n    file.write('\\\\n')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
